## NOW

### NOW-001: Jenn-only R5 scanner module-lifecycle correction start decision

```text
requires_jenn_decision=true
decision_owner=Jenn
execution_authorized=false
```

R4's independent review found that a hash-matching scanner can retain a delayed
thread and reinstall the fixed `sys.modules` mapping after the loader returns.
R5 may close only that post-return lifecycle escape. It must preserve R1–R4
bytes and remain entirely offline.

The earlier R3 actual execution decision was consumed exactly once and ended
`BLOCKED_REVIEW_BINDING_MISMATCH` at scanner load. It cannot be retried or
treated as an open execution gate.

